{title: 198 - And Can It Be?}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #198 • SAGINA • 17.15.16.16}
{lyricist: Charles Wesley}
{composer: Thomas Campbell}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 198}
{meta: tune SAGINA}
{meta: meter 17.15.16.16}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G/D]And can it be [Bm]that [Am]Ishould [D/F#]gain [G]an interest [D/F#]in [G]the [Am/C]Savior's [D/A]blood!
[D/F#]Died he for me, [Em/B]who caused [D/A]his pain! [G]For me [F#dim]who [G]him [C/G]to [G]death [C/G]pursued?
[G]Amazing love! How can [F#dim]it [D/F#]be [F#dim]that [G]Thou, [C/G]my God, [Am]shouldst [D/A]die for me?
[G]Amazing love! How [C/G]can [Am]it [D/A]be that Thou, [G]my God, shouldst [F#dim]die [D/F#]for me?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[C]Amazing [Bm]love! How [C]can it be
[G]that thou, [Am]my God, [Em/B]shouldst die [D/A]for [G]me?
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G/D]He left [Am]his [D/A]Father's [Am/E]throne [G]above
[D/F#]so free, [Em/B]so [D/A]infinite [G]his grace!;
[D/F#]emptied himself of [G]all but love,
[G]and bled for [F#dim]Adam's [C/G]helpless [D]race.
[G]'Tis mercy [F#dim]all, immense [Am]and [D]free,
[G]for O my [Am]God, [D/F#]it [G]found out [D/F#]me!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G/D]Long my [Am]imprisoned [D/F#]sprit [Em/B]lay,
[D/F#]fast bound [Em/B]in sin [D/F#]and [G]nature's night;
[D/F#]thine eye [Em/B]diffused [D/F#]a [G]quickening ray;
[G]I woke, the [F#dim]dungeon [C/G]flamed [Am]with [D]light;
[G]my chains fell [F#dim]off, my [C/G]heart [Am]was [D]free,
[G]I rose, went [Am]forth, [D/F#]and [G]followed [D/F#]thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G/D]No condemnation [Am/E]now [G]I [Em/B]dread;
[D/F#]Jesus, [Em/B]and [D/A]all [G]in him, is mine;
[D/F#]alive [Em/B]in [D/A]him, [G]my living Head,
[G]and clothed in [F#dim]righteousnes [Am]divine,
[G]bold I [F#dim]approach [D/F#]th' [G]eternal [D]throne,
[G]and claim the [Am]crown, [D/F#]through [G]Christ my [D/F#]own.
{end_of_verse}
